    doi = "10.1080/03017605.2017.1412623",
    note = "CORE ARGUMENT: Reconstructs Capital's genesis and structure from Marx's 1860s biography and the MEGA manuscripts, explaining why the initial six-book plan changed. MARX-CENTRALITY: Title and main topic: the writing of Capital.",
    keywords = "MEGA, plan-of-capital, genesis, High, METADATA\\_CLEANED: number",
    abstract = "The debate on the structure of Marx's Capital, and on the probable explanations for the changes he made to the initial ‘six books plan’, has always been a relevant topic in Marxist studies. This article provides a more exhaustive account of the genesis of Capital, on the basis of a revisitation of Marx's intellectual biography during the 1860s, and of the publication of all preparatory manuscripts of Marx's magnum opus, recently appeared in the MEGA2, the historical-critical edition of the complete works of Marx and Engels.",
